@*
    ── בית — Mentor Home ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Data source: IMentorWorkspaceService.LoadAsync() — one snapshot carrying
                 GET /api/mentor/attention, the mentor's projects, the open
                 requests on them and the mentor's own personal tasks.
                 IMentorWorkspaceService.BuildCalendarAsync for the dates.

    ── THE LECTURER DASHBOARD, MINUS LECTURER RESPONSIBILITIES ──────────────
    This screen and /dashboard/lecturer are ONE dashboard drawn twice. They
    share their composition, their card language, their row rhythm, their
    empty states, their fill behaviour and their breakpoints, and they share
    them literally: every one of those lives in css/motiva-dashboard.css and
    neither page owns a copy. What differs is WHICH ITEMS each card selects.

        WIDE (1.75fr)   דורש פעולה · הצוותים שלי
        RAIL (1fr)      מועדים קרובים · משימות אישיות

    ── WHAT A MENTOR IS NOT RESPONSIBLE FOR ─────────────────────────────────
    The lecturer's middle card is תמונת מצב צוותים — every team IN THE COURSE,
    with a summary line counting the whole cohort and a "בהנחייתי" tag marking
    the subset that is personally theirs. None of that is meaningful here: a
    mentor's population IS their own teams, so

      • there is no course-wide count, no "צוותים בקורס", no "ללא מנחה משויך"
        and no risk aggregate — those are שיבוצים and lecturer questions;
      • there is no "בהנחייתי" qualifier, because it would be telling the
        reader something this screen cannot contradict;
      • there is no mentor name on a row. Every row is this mentor's.

    Nothing decorative replaced them. The card is shorter, which is the honest
    result of a smaller responsibility.

    ── דורש פעולה IS THE MENTOR'S OWN WORK QUEUE ────────────────────────────
    Same card, same lift, same filter tabs, same row density as the lecturer's
    — different rows. Two kinds only, and both are ENTITIES whose current
    workflow state requires this mentor:

      הגשה   MentorAttentionKind.Submission — a TaskSubmission waiting on this
             mentor's review
      בקשה   MentorAttentionKind.Request — a ProjectRequest awaiting this
             mentor's recommendation

    Both come from GET /api/mentor/attention, which is the product's single
    source of truth for "what is waiting on this mentor" — this page does not
    filter by status, compute an age or compare against a threshold, and the
    daily digest reads the very same model. An item leaves the queue when the
    underlying entity moves; nothing here is marked done.

    PERSONAL TASKS ARE NOT IN IT. The attention model does carry the mentor's
    overdue reminders, and they are filtered out here for the reason the
    lecturer's queue gives: a note you wrote yourself is not the system waiting
    on you, and mixing the two puts two kinds of completion in one list. They
    have their own card, with a checkbox.

    ── ROWS INSPECT, THEY DO NOT NAVIGATE ───────────────────────────────────
    The one deliberate behavioural difference from the lecturer's queue, and it
    is the mentor experience's existing rule rather than a new idea: clicking an
    entity on a mentor overview opens its shared popup OVER this page, and only
    the CTA inside that popup changes the URL. So these rows are MRow with
    OnClick (a <button>) where the lecturer's are MRow with Href (an <a>). The
    affordance is identical — badge, title, context, an action verb and a
    chevron — and both render through the same MRow and the same stylesheet.

    ── WHAT THIS PASS REMOVED FROM THIS SCREEN ──────────────────────────────
    All of it because the lecturer dashboard does not have it and the two are
    one product:

      the hand-rolled .mh-* card / head / row / accordion system   → M* + mdash-*
      the two shortcut pills under the greeting                    → the queue's
                                                                     filter tabs
                                                                     state the
                                                                     same counts
      the per-team attention ACCORDION                             → one row per
                                                                     item, as the
                                                                     lecturer has
      the colour key under the dashboard                           → the rail's
                                                                     tiles read
                                                                     the same way
                                                                     on both roles
*@
@page "/dashboard/mentor"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Mentor + "," + Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff)]
@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Mentor
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@inject IMentorWorkspaceService Workspace
@inject IPersonalTasksService PersonalTasks
@inject IRoadmapStagesService Roadmap
@inject NavigationManager Nav

<div class="mdash-page" dir="rtl">

    @* The greeting and nothing else — the lecturer header's own rule. The
       workload sentence and the two shortcut pills that used to sit here
       stated counts that the queue's filter tabs now carry on the card
       that owns them. *@
    <MPageHeader Variant="MPageHeader.HeaderVariant.Hero"
                 Class="mdash-header"
                 Title="@_greeting" />

    @if (_loading)
    {
        <MLoadingState Label="טוענת את סביבת העבודה…" />
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="mdash-grid">

            @* ── The wide column — what needs me, and how my teams are ── *@
            <div class="mdash-main-col">

            @* ── 1. דורש פעולה ─────────────────────────────────────
                 The page's one lifted card, and the one glyph that is not
                 the brand sweep — both read the shared stylesheet's
                 .mdash-card-strong / .mdash-head-icon-alert, so the
                 emphasis is the same emphasis the lecturer's queue has. *@
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None"
                   Class="mdash-card-strong mdash-queue-card">
                <div class="sd-head">
                    <span class="sd-head-icon mdash-head-icon-alert" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <path d="M10.3 3.9 1.8 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h17a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3L13.7 3.9a2 2 0 0 0-3.4 0z"></path>
                            <path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="sd-head-title mdash-queue-title">דורש פעולה</h2>

                    @if (WorkQueue.Count > 0)
                    {
                        <div class="mdash-head-tabs">
                            <MFilterTabs Tabs="@FilterTabs"
                                         ActiveKey="@_filter"
                                         OnSelect="@(k => _filter = k)"
                                         AriaLabel="סינון תור העבודה" />
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>

                @if (WorkQueue.Count == 0)
                {
                    <MEmptyState Title="אין פריטים שממתינים לפעולה שלך."
                                 Description="הגשות לבדיקה ובקשות שממתינות להמלצתך יופיעו כאן מעצמן." />
                }
                else if (VisibleQueue.Count == 0)
                {
                    <MEmptyState Title="אין פריטים בסינון הזה."
                                 Description="אפשר לחזור ל״הכל״ כדי לראות את שאר התור." />
                }
                else
                {
                    <MRowList Class="mdash-queue-list" AriaLabel="פריטים שדורשים את פעולתך">
                        @foreach (var item in VisibleQueue.Take(QueuePreview))
                        {
                            var it = item;
                            <MRow Class="mdash-queue-row"
                                  Primary="@it.Title"
                                  Secondary="@it.Context"
                                  OnClick="@(_ => OpenAttentionItem(it.Source))"
                                  AriaLabel="@($"{it.TypeLabel}: {it.Title}. {it.Context}. {it.ActionLabel}")">
                                <Leading>
                                    <MStatusBadge Size="MStatusBadge.BadgeSize.Small"
                                                  Variant="@it.TypeVariant"
                                                  Text="@it.TypeLabel" />
                                </Leading>
                                <Trailing>
                                    <span class="mdash-go">
                                        @it.ActionLabel
                                        <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none"
                                             stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.3" stroke-linecap="round"
                                             stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                            <path d="M15 6l-6 6 6 6"></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    </span>
                                </Trailing>
                            </MRow>
                        }
                    </MRowList>
                }

                @* Both destinations exist and neither is the queue itself, so
                   the foot only appears when the preview is actually hiding
                   something — the lecturer card's own rule. *@
                @if (VisibleQueue.Count > QueuePreview)
                {
                    <div class="mdash-card-foot">
                        <a class="mdash-foot-link" href="@MentorLinks.RequestsInbox">
                            לכל הבקשות
                            @if (RequestItems.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="mdash-foot-n">@RequestItems.Count</span>
                            }
                        </a>
                        <a class="mdash-foot-link" href="@MentorLinks.Reviews">
                            לכל ההגשות
                            @if (SubmissionItems.Count > 0)
                            {
                                <span class="mdash-foot-n">@SubmissionItems.Count</span>
                            }
                        </a>
                    </div>
                }
            </MCard>

            @* ── 2. הצוותים שלי ────────────────────────────────────
                 EVERY supervised team, worst-first — not only the ones in
                 trouble. That is the difference from the lecturer's card
                 and it is the whole reason this one keeps a possessive
                 title: the lecturer previews EXCEPTIONS out of a cohort
                 too large to list, while a mentor's caseload is small
                 enough to be the list.

                 NO SUMMARY LINE. The lecturer's MSummaryTag counts the
                 course; there is no such population here, and counting
                 "my teams" beside a list of my teams says nothing. *@
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Class="mdash-teams-card">
                <div class="sd-head">
                    <span class="sd-head-icon motiva-ico-gradient" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#motivaIconGradient)"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path>
                            <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"></circle>
                            <path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="sd-head-title">הצוותים שלי</h2>
                    <a class="sd-head-link" href="@MentorLinks.Projects()">לכל הצוותים</a>
                </div>

                @if (TeamRows.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="mdash-teams-calm">
                        <span class="mdash-teams-calm-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        לא משויכים אליך פרויקטים כרגע.
                    </p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <MRowList Class="mdash-team-list" AriaLabel="הצוותים שלי">
                        @foreach (var t in TeamRows.Take(TeamsPreview))
                        {
                            var team = t;
                            <MRow Class="mdash-team-row"
                                  Primary="@team.Name"
                                  Secondary="@team.Context"
                                  Meta="@team.Reason"
                                  MetaTone="@team.ReasonTone"
                                  OnClick="@(_ => OpenProject(team.ProjectId))"
                                  AriaLabel="@($"פתיחת פרטי {team.Name} — {team.Reason}")">
                                <Leading>
                                    @* Decorative: the row's aria-label already
                                       names the state this dot encodes. *@
                                    <MStatusDot Tone="@team.Tone" />
                                </Leading>
                            </MRow>
                        }
                    </MRowList>

                    @if (TeamRows.Count > TeamsPreview)
                    {
                        <p class="mdash-teams-more">@MoreTeamsLabel(TeamRows.Count - TeamsPreview)</p>
                    }
                }
            </MCard>

            </div>

            @* ── The rail — what is coming, and what I set myself ── *@
            <div class="mdash-side-col">

            @* ── 3. מועדים קרובים ──────────────────────────────────
                 The same tile card the lecturer draws, from the mentor's
                 OWN dates: BuildCalendarAsync composes them from this
                 mentor's projects only, so nothing course-wide and nothing
                 invented can reach it. Same builder /mentor/calendar uses,
                 so a date reads identically in both places. *@
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Class="mdash-dates-card">
                <div class="sd-head">
                    <span class="sd-head-icon motiva-ico-gradient" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#motivaIconGradient)"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="3"></rect>
                            <path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="sd-head-title" id="mdash-dates-h">מועדים קרובים</h2>
                    <a class="sd-head-link" href="@MentorLinks.Calendar">ליומן המלא</a>
                </div>

                @if (_upcomingLoading)
                {
                    <p class="mdash-dates-empty">
                        <strong>טוענת מועדים…</strong>
                        <span>המועדים הקרובים יופיעו כאן בעוד רגע.</span>
                    </p>
                }
                else if (_upcoming.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="mdash-dates-empty">
                        <strong>אין מועדים קרובים</strong>
                        <span>המועד הבא יופיע כאן כשייקבע.</span>
                    </p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="mdash-up-list">
                        @foreach (var e in _upcoming)
                        {
                            var ev = e;
                            <button type="button"
                                    class="@($"mdash-up-row mdash-kind-{MentorEventTypes.CssSuffix(ev.Type)}")"
                                    @onclick="@(() => OpenEvent(ev))"
                                    aria-label="@($"פתיחת {ev.Title}")">
                                <span class="mdash-up-tile">
                                    <span class="mdash-up-day">@ev.Date.Day.ToString("00")</span>
                                    <span class="mdash-up-month">@MotivaDates.ShortMonth(ev.Date)</span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="mdash-up-body">
                                    <span class="mdash-up-title" title="@ev.Title">@ev.Title</span>
                                    <span class="mdash-up-meta">@UpcomingRelative(ev) · @UpcomingContext(ev)</span>
                                </span>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </MCard>

            @* ── 4. משימות אישיות ──────────────────────────────────
                 The lecturer card, unchanged in concept: the mentor's own
                 reminders, created / edited / completed / deleted through
                 the same IPersonalTasksService and the same
                 MentorPersonalTaskModal every other mentor screen uses.

                 IT LINKS NOWHERE, deliberately. Home IS the mentor's
                 personal-task surface now — המשימות שלי has left the nav
                 exactly as it left the lecturer's, so a "לכל המשימות" link
                 would point at a destination the product no longer offers. *@
            <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Class="mdash-tasks-card">
                <div class="sd-head">
                    <span class="sd-head-icon motiva-ico-gradient" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#motivaIconGradient)"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <path d="M9 11l3 3L22 4"></path>
                            <path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="sd-head-title">משימות אישיות</h2>
                    @if (ActiveTasks.Count > 0)
                    {
                        <span class="motiva-count mdash-head-count"
                              aria-label="@($"{ActiveTasks.Count} משימות פתוחות")">@ActiveTasks.Count</span>
                    }
                </div>

                @if (ActiveTasks.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="mdash-tasks-calm">
                        <span class="mdash-tasks-calm-mark" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
                        הכול בוצע
                    </p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <MRowList Class="mdash-tasks-list" AriaLabel="משימות אישיות">
                        @foreach (var t in ActiveTasks.Take(TasksPreview))
                        {
                            var task = t;
                            <MRow Class="mdash-task-row"
                                  Secondary="@DueLabel(task)"
                                  MetaTone="MRow.RowMetaTone.Default">
                                <Leading>
                                    <button type="button"
                                            class="mdash-check"
                                            disabled="@(_togglingId == task.Id)"
                                            @onclick="@(() => ToggleTaskAsync(task))"
                                            aria-label="@($"סימון \"{task.Title}\" כהושלמה")">
                                        <span class="mdash-check-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                    </button>
                                </Leading>
                                <PrimaryContent>
                                    <button type="button" class="mdash-task-title"
                                            @onclick="@(() => OpenTask(task))"
                                            title="@task.Title"
                                            aria-label="@($"עריכת המשימה {task.Title}")">@task.Title</button>
                                </PrimaryContent>
                            </MRow>
                        }
                    </MRowList>

                    @if (ActiveTasks.Count > TasksPreview)
                    {
                        <p class="mdash-tasks-more">@MoreTasksLabel(ActiveTasks.Count - TasksPreview)</p>
                    }
                }

                <div class="mdash-card-foot">
                    <button type="button" class="mdash-add" @onclick="OpenNewTask">
                        <span class="mdash-add-glyph" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
                        <span>משימה</span>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </MCard>

            </div>

        </div>
    }
</div>

@*  ── Inspection popups, all opened OVER this dashboard ────────────────────
    The mentor rule this screen follows: clicking an entity on an overview
    INSPECTS it here; only the CTA inside the popup navigates. None of these is
    a page-local implementation — the Quick View is the same panel
    פרויקטים בהנחייתי opens, the request modal is the same one the mentor
    request queue opens, and the task editor is the same one יומן ותכנון and
    the lecturer dashboard open. *@
<MentorProjectQuickView Card="@_openProject"
                        Focus="@_openProjectFocus"
                        OnClose="CloseProject" />

<MentorRequestModal RequestId="@_openRequestId"
                    WaitingLabel="@OpenRequestWaitingLabel"
                    OnClose="@(() => _openRequestId = null)"
                    OnChanged="ReloadAsync" />

<MentorPersonalTaskModal IsOpen="@(_creatingTask || _openTask is not null)"
                         EditingTask="@_openTask"
                         Projects="@_ws.Projects"
                         OnClose="CloseTaskEditor"
                         OnSaved="@(_ => TaskChangedAsync())"
                         OnDeleted="@(_ => TaskChangedAsync())" />

@code {
    [CascadingParameter] private User? _user { get; set; }

    // ── Preview depths ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // The lecturer dashboard's caps, and for its reasons: they are measured
    // against the same grid, the same row metrics and the same viewport bands,
    // which are all in css/motiva-dashboard.css. The one that differs is the
    // team preview — see TeamsPreview.
    private const int QueuePreview    = 4;
    private const int UpcomingPreview = 3;
    private const int TasksPreview    = 4;

    /// <summary>How many teams the middle card lists. FOUR, where the
    /// lecturer's card shows three.
    ///
    /// <para>Not a style difference: the lecturer previews the EXCEPTIONS out
    /// of a cohort that a card could never hold, so a fourth row buys almost
    /// nothing and the CTA is the real answer. A mentor's list is their entire
    /// caseload, so each extra row is a larger share of the whole — four is
    /// what the card's own height holds at the base density, and the "ועוד N"
    /// line states the remainder honestly.</para></summary>
    private const int TeamsPreview = 4;

    private MentorWorkspace _ws = MentorWorkspace.Empty;
    private bool _loading = true;

    private List<MentorCalendarEvent> _upcoming = new();

    /// <summary>מועדים קרובים fills in after the rest of the screen — see
    /// LoadUpcomingAsync.</summary>
    private bool _upcomingLoading = true;

    /// <summary>The task whose checkbox is mid-flight, so it cannot be pressed
    /// twice while the PATCH is on the wire.</summary>
    private int? _togglingId;

    /// <summary>The queue's lens: "" for everything, "submissions",
    /// "requests". Presentational only — it hides rows the card already holds
    /// and touches no feed, filter or count.</summary>
    private string _filter = "";

    // ── Inspection state ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // WHY THESE ARE FIELDS AND NOT ROUTES. Every one of them used to be an
    // href, and each of those navigations then opened a popup on ARRIVAL — one
    // click cost the mentor the screen they were reading in order to show a
    // panel that could just as well have opened here. The destinations are all
    // still reachable: each popup carries the CTA that goes there, and that CTA
    // is the only thing on this screen that changes the URL.

    /// <summary>The project whose Quick View is open, or null.</summary>
    private MentorProjectCard? _openProject;

    /// <summary>The attention row the mentor clicked, when the Quick View was
    /// opened from one. It decides which submission the panel names and where
    /// its primary CTA goes, so clicking the second of two waiting submissions
    /// does not offer the first.</summary>
    private MentorAttentionItemDto? _openProjectFocus;

    private int?             _openRequestId;
    private PersonalTaskDto? _openTask;

    /// <summary>True while the shared editor is open on a NEW reminder — the
    /// same field cannot express "creating" and "editing nothing", so this
    /// does. Same contract as the lecturer dashboard's.</summary>
    private bool _creatingTask;

    /// <summary>Roadmap progress per project, for the Quick View's stage line.
    /// Loaded in the BACKGROUND, like the dates and for the same reason: this
    /// dashboard paints from one fast snapshot, and holding it behind a second
    /// round-trip to fill one line of a panel that is not open yet would be
    /// paying for it on every visit.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyDictionary<int, ProjectRoadmapProgressDto> _roadmap =
        new Dictionary<int, ProjectRoadmapProgressDto>();

    /// <summary>Waiting phrase for the request currently open, taken from the
    /// same attention item the row rendered — so the modal and the row it was
    /// opened from cannot word one request two ways.</summary>
    private string? OpenRequestWaitingLabel =>
        _openRequestId is int id
            ? _ws.AwaitingMe.FirstOrDefault(r => r.EntityId == id)?.WaitingLabel
            : null;

    // ── Time / greeting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private string _greeting
    {
        get
        {
            var name = _user?.FirstName?.Trim();
            var hour = DateTime.Now.Hour;

            // Written as conditionals rather than as a `switch { < 12 => … }`
            // relational pattern on purpose: inside a .razor @code block the
            // Razor parser reads a leading `<` as the start of a tag and the
            // whole code block stops compiling.
            var part = hour < 12 ? "בוקר טוב"
                     : hour < 17 ? "צהריים טובים"
                     : hour < 21 ? "ערב טוב"
                     :             "לילה טוב";

            return string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) ? part : $"{part}, {name}";
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() => await ReloadAsync();

    private async Task ReloadAsync()
    {
        _loading = true;
        _ws = await Workspace.LoadAsync();
        _loading = false;

        // NOT awaited, and deliberately so. BuildCalendarAsync issues one
        // GetProjectDetailAsync per project on top of the snapshot — it is what
        // makes /mentor/calendar take the better part of ten seconds on a full
        // caseload. Awaiting it here would hold the ENTIRE screen behind the one
        // card that needs it, so Home paints from the single fast snapshot and
        // מועדים קרובים fills itself in a moment later.
        _ = LoadUpcomingAsync();
        _ = LoadRoadmapAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>The mentor's own dates, from the same builder /mentor/calendar
    /// renders. Floored at today: an undated entry cannot be "coming up", and a
    /// past one is not either.</summary>
    private async Task LoadUpcomingAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var today  = DateTime.Today;
            var events = await Workspace.BuildCalendarAsync(_ws);

            _upcoming = events
                .Where(e => e.Date.Date >= today)
                .OrderBy(e => e.Date)
                .Take(UpcomingPreview)
                .ToList();
        }
        catch
        {
            // A failed calendar build empties one card; it must not take the
            // screen down with it. The empty state says so honestly.
            _upcoming = new();
        }
        finally
        {
            _upcomingLoading = false;
            await InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Roadmap progress, off the critical path. Same contract as
    /// LoadUpcomingAsync: it fills a detail in, it never gates the paint, and a
    /// failure leaves the fallback wording rather than an error.</summary>
    private async Task LoadRoadmapAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var entries = await Roadmap.GetMentorProjectsProgressAsync()
                          ?? new List<MentorRoadmapEntryDto>();

            _roadmap = entries.GroupBy(e => e.ProjectId)
                              .ToDictionary(g => g.Key, g => g.First().Progress);
        }
        catch
        {
            _roadmap = new Dictionary<int, ProjectRoadmapProgressDto>();
        }

        await InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
    }

    // ── 1. דורש פעולה — the mentor's system work queue ───────────────────────

    /// <summary>One queue row. Every field is DERIVED from the entity's current
    /// state on each render — there is no stored work item, so there is nothing
    /// to keep in sync and nothing to mark done. <c>Source</c> is the attention
    /// item itself, because the row INSPECTS rather than navigates and the
    /// popups need the item, not a URL.</summary>
    private sealed record WorkItem(
        MentorAttentionKind       Kind,
        string                    TypeLabel,
        MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant TypeVariant,
        string                    Title,
        string                    Context,
        string                    ActionLabel,
        MentorAttentionItemDto    Source);

    /// <summary>Submissions waiting on this mentor's review.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> SubmissionItems => _ws.Reviews;

    /// <summary>Requests awaiting this mentor's recommendation.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> RequestItems => _ws.AwaitingMe;

    /// <summary>
    /// The two feeds as one queue, IN THE SERVER'S OWN ORDER.
    ///
    /// <para>No .Where on status, no .OrderBy on a timestamp and no threshold
    /// comparison: GET /api/mentor/attention already returns worst-first
    /// (NeedsAttention → Waiting → New, oldest first inside each) and this only
    /// drops the kind that belongs on another card. That is what keeps this
    /// screen, the mentor request queue and the daily digest agreeing about
    /// which item is most pressing.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>PERSONAL TASKS ARE DROPPED HERE, and only here — the model still
    /// carries them and משימות אישיות still lists them. A reminder is not the
    /// system waiting on the mentor; it is the mentor waiting on themselves,
    /// and it is completed by a person ticking a box rather than by a workflow
    /// moving somewhere else.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<WorkItem> WorkQueue =>
        _ws.Attention.Items
            .Where(i => i.Kind is MentorAttentionKind.Submission or MentorAttentionKind.Request)
            .Select(i => new WorkItem(
                Kind:        i.Kind,
                // The lecturer queue's two words, not MentorAttentionRows'
                // longer "הגשה לבדיקה": the badge names the KIND and the
                // trailing verb says what is done about it, so repeating
                // "לבדיקה" in both would be the same word twice on one row.
                TypeLabel:   i.Kind == MentorAttentionKind.Submission ? "הגשה" : "בקשה",
                TypeVariant: MentorAttentionRows.TypeVariant(i),
                Title:       i.Title,
                Context:     QueueContext(i),
                // A mentor RECOMMENDS on a request; only a lecturer decides
                // one. The verb is the difference between the two queues, and
                // it is the mentor's own vocabulary — MentorProjectSignals
                // words the same state "בקשה ממתינה להמלצתך".
                ActionLabel: i.Kind == MentorAttentionKind.Submission ? "לבדיקה" : "להמלצה",
                Source:      i))
            .ToList();

    private IReadOnlyList<WorkItem> VisibleQueue => _filter switch
    {
        "requests"    => WorkQueue.Where(i => i.Kind == MentorAttentionKind.Request).ToList(),
        "submissions" => WorkQueue.Where(i => i.Kind == MentorAttentionKind.Submission).ToList(),
        _             => WorkQueue,
    };

    /// <summary>The lens, carrying each kind's size. A zero renders no bubble,
    /// which is MFilterTabs' own rule.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MFilterTabs.Tab> FilterTabs => new[]
    {
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("",            "הכל",   WorkQueue.Count),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("requests",    "בקשות", RequestItems.Count),
        new MFilterTabs.Tab("submissions", "הגשות", SubmissionItems.Count),
    };

    /// <summary>The row's context line: whose it is, how long it has waited,
    /// and the milestone when the item has one.
    ///
    /// <para>A WAIT, never "באיחור" — neither a submission nor a request has a
    /// deadline it could be late for, which is the rule
    /// <see cref="MentorAttentionRows.TimeLabel"/> exists to enforce. The
    /// waiting phrase is the server's own pre-rendered
    /// <c>WaitingLabel</c>.</para></summary>
    private static string QueueContext(MentorAttentionItemDto i)
    {
        var stage = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(i.MilestoneTitle) ? null : i.MilestoneTitle;
        return Join(MentorAttentionRows.Team(i), i.WaitingLabel, stage);
    }

    // ── 2. הצוותים שלי ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private sealed record TeamItem(
        int ProjectId, string Name, string Context, string Reason,
        MStatusDot.DotTone Tone, MRow.RowMetaTone ReasonTone);

    /// <summary>
    /// Every supervised team, worst-first.
    ///
    /// <para>Order is the shared signal priority then the nearest deadline —
    /// the same ordering פרויקטים בהנחייתי uses, so the top of this list is the
    /// top of that screen. It does NOT exclude the teams that also appear in
    /// דורש פעולה: the two cards answer different questions (what is blocked on
    /// me, versus how are my teams) and the same team legitimately appears in
    /// both answers.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<TeamItem> TeamRows =>
        _ws.Projects
           .OrderBy(p => MentorProjectSignals.Priority(SignalOf(p)))
           .ThenBy(p => p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate ?? DateTime.MaxValue)
           .Select(BuildTeamItem)
           .ToList();

    /// <summary>
    /// The project's signal, from the three real columns.
    ///
    /// <para><b>Why this is not Projects.HealthStatus.</b> That column is never
    /// written by this application, so in practice every project comes back
    /// OnTrack and the row would draw a calm dot beside a milestone that is
    /// visibly overdue. The state is read off real columns instead, through the
    /// shared <see cref="MentorProjectSignal"/> — the same vocabulary
    /// פרויקטים בהנחייתי filters and colours its rows with.</para></summary>
    private MentorProjectSignal SignalOf(MentorProjectSummaryDto p) =>
        MentorProjectSignals.Of(
            milestoneOverdue: MentorTime.IsOverdue(p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate),
            pendingReviews:   p.PendingMentorReview,
            openRequests:     _ws.OpenRequestsFor(p.Id));

    /// <summary>
    /// One team row: the team, its current stage and deadline, and what it
    /// needs next.
    ///
    /// <para><b>NO MENTOR NAME.</b> The lecturer's equivalent row ends its
    /// context with "מנחה: …" because that card spans the whole course and the
    /// reader genuinely does not know whose team it is. Every row here is this
    /// mentor's, so the line carries the project, the milestone and its date
    /// instead — three facts the reader cannot derive.</para>
    ///
    /// <para><b>OVERDUE TASKS OUTRANK THE SIGNAL.</b> A team carrying work past
    /// its due date is the strongest thing this row can say, and it is the one
    /// state on this card that earns rose — the same rule the lecturer's team
    /// rows follow. Everything else takes MentorProjectSignals.Note, the
    /// product's single wording for "what does this project need from me
    /// next".</para></summary>
    private TeamItem BuildTeamItem(MentorProjectSummaryDto p)
    {
        var signal  = SignalOf(p);
        bool overdue = p.OverdueTasks > 0;

        // Correct Hebrew number agreement: never "1 משימות באיחור".
        string reason = overdue
            ? (p.OverdueTasks == 1 ? "משימה אחת באיחור" : $"{p.OverdueTasks} משימות באיחור")
            : MentorProjectSignals.Note(
                  signal, p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate,
                  p.PendingMentorReview, _ws.OpenRequestList(p.Id));

        var context = new List<string>();
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.Title))                  context.Add(p.Title);
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle))  context.Add(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle!);
        if (p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate is { } due)                 context.Add($"יעד {due:dd.MM}");

        return new TeamItem(
            ProjectId:  p.Id,
            Name:       string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.TeamName) ? p.Title : p.TeamName,
            Context:    string.Join(" · ", context),
            Reason:     reason,
            Tone:       overdue ? MStatusDot.DotTone.Rose : MentorProjectSignals.Tone(signal),
            ReasonTone: overdue ? MRow.RowMetaTone.Rose   : MRow.RowMetaTone.Default);
    }

    // ── 3. מועדים קרובים ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>The team the entry belongs to. A mentor's own reminder has
    /// none, and says so rather than printing a blank line.</summary>
    private static string UpcomingContext(MentorCalendarEvent e)
    {
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(e.TeamName))     return e.TeamName;
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(e.ProjectTitle)) return e.ProjectTitle;
        return "תזכורת אישית";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// How far off it is, in words — "היום", "מחר", "בעוד 5 ימים".
    ///
    /// <para>The hour rides along when there IS one.
    /// <c>MentorCalendarEvent.HasTime</c> is true for exactly one thing — a
    /// mentor personal task whose owner filled in שעת התחלה — so a real slot is
    /// never dropped and one is never invented.</para></summary>
    private static string UpcomingRelative(MentorCalendarEvent e)
    {
        var days = (e.Date.Date - DateTime.Today).Days;

        var when = days switch
        {
            0 => "היום",
            1 => "מחר",
            2 => "בעוד יומיים",
            _ => $"בעוד {days} ימים",
        };

        return e.HasTime ? $"{when} · {e.Date:HH:mm}" : when;
    }

    // ── 4. משימות אישיות ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>ACTIVE reminders, soonest first. <c>IsDone</c> is the existing
    /// completion flag and a ticked reminder is finished work, so it simply
    /// leaves this list. The order is the lecturer card's: by due date
    /// ascending with undated tasks last, which is what
    /// <c>DateTime.MaxValue</c> buys.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PersonalTaskDto> ActiveTasks =>
        _ws.PersonalTasks
            .Where(t => !t.IsDone)
            .OrderBy(t => t.DueDate ?? DateTime.MaxValue)
            .ThenByDescending(t => t.CreatedAt)
            .ToList();

    /// <summary>A reminder's one line: when it is due, and the project it
    /// belongs to when it has one. "באיחור" is allowed HERE and nowhere else on
    /// this page — a reminder is the only thing on Home carrying a date its
    /// owner chose, so it is the only thing that can be late.</summary>
    private static string DueLabel(PersonalTaskDto t)
    {
        var where = OneOf(t.TeamName, t.ProjectTitle);
        if (t.DueDate is not { } due) return Join("ללא תאריך יעד", where);

        int days = (DateTime.Today - due.Date).Days;
        var when = days switch
        {
            > 1 => $"באיחור {days} ימים",
            1   => "באיחור יום",
            0   => "היום",
            -1  => "מחר",
            _   => $"עד {due:dd.MM}",
        };
        return Join(when, where);
    }

    // ── Create, complete, edit ───────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // ALL FOUR OPERATIONS ARE THE EXISTING ONES. IPersonalTasksService and
    // MentorPersonalTaskModal are what /mentor/tasks, /mentor/calendar and the
    // lecturer dashboard already use; this page adds no model, no endpoint, no
    // table and no second editor.

    private void OpenNewTask()
    {
        _openTask     = null;
        _creatingTask = true;
    }

    /// <summary>The shared personal-task editor.</summary>
    private void OpenTask(PersonalTaskDto? task)
    {
        _creatingTask = false;
        _openTask     = task;
    }

    private void CloseTaskEditor()
    {
        _openTask     = null;
        _creatingTask = false;
    }

    /// <summary>A save or a delete closes the editor and re-reads the snapshot,
    /// so the queue, the team notes and the task list all move together rather
    /// than one of them going stale.</summary>
    private async Task TaskChangedAsync()
    {
        CloseTaskEditor();
        await ReloadAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Complete one reminder, against the endpoint every other screen calls.
    ///
    /// <para>PATCH …/personal-tasks/{id}/toggle, whose UPDATE carries
    /// <c>AND UserId = @@UserId</c> so ownership is structural rather than a
    /// check this page could get wrong. The flag is flipped locally afterwards
    /// rather than refetching the snapshot to learn one bit; the row then fails
    /// the <c>!IsDone</c> filter and leaves the card on the next
    /// render.</para></summary>
    private async Task ToggleTaskAsync(PersonalTaskDto task)
    {
        if (_togglingId is not null) return;

        _togglingId = task.Id;
        var ok = await PersonalTasks.ToggleAsync(task.Id);
        _togglingId = null;

        if (ok) task.IsDone = !task.IsDone;
    }

    // ── Opening an entity, in place ─────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>Opens one project's Quick View over this dashboard.</summary>
    private void OpenProject(int projectId, MentorAttentionItemDto? focus = null)
    {
        var project = _ws.Projects.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Id == projectId);

        // A project the snapshot does not carry cannot be summarised honestly,
        // so fall back to the route rather than opening an empty panel.
        if (project is null)
        {
            Nav.NavigateTo(focus?.Href ?? $"/mentor/projects/{projectId}");
            return;
        }

        _openProjectFocus = focus;
        _openProject      = MentorProjectCard.Build(_ws, project, _roadmap.GetValueOrDefault(projectId));
    }

    private void CloseProject()
    {
        _openProject      = null;
        _openProjectFocus = null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// One queue row, opened in the popup that owns its kind.
    ///
    /// <para>A request opens the shared request modal. A submission opens the
    /// project's Quick View FOCUSED on it: the mentor sees which submission is
    /// waiting and how long it has waited without leaving the dashboard, and
    /// the panel's primary CTA is that submission's own review screen. There is
    /// no shared review popup to mount here — the review drawer belongs to
    /// מרחב הפרויקט — and inventing a second one is exactly the duplication
    /// this pass removes.</para></summary>
    private void OpenAttentionItem(MentorAttentionItemDto item)
    {
        switch (item.Kind)
        {
            case MentorAttentionKind.Request:
                _openRequestId = item.EntityId;
                break;

            default:
                if (item.ProjectId is int pid) OpenProject(pid, item);
                else Nav.NavigateTo(item.Href);
                break;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>One מועדים קרובים row, opened in place like everything else on
    /// this screen. A milestone or a dated deliverable is not an entity a
    /// mentor opens — it is a date ON a project, so the project is what the
    /// panel shows.</summary>
    private void OpenEvent(MentorCalendarEvent e)
    {
        switch (e.Type)
        {
            case MentorEventType.PersonalTask:
            case MentorEventType.Meeting:
                var task = _ws.PersonalTasks.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == e.EntityId);
                if (task is null) Nav.NavigateTo(MentorLinks.Calendar);
                else              OpenTask(task);
                break;

            case MentorEventType.Review when e.ProjectId is int reviewPid:
                OpenProject(reviewPid, _ws.Reviews.FirstOrDefault(r => r.EntityId == e.EntityId));
                break;

            default:
                if (e.ProjectId is int pid) OpenProject(pid);
                else                        Nav.NavigateTo(e.Href ?? MentorLinks.Calendar);
                break;
        }
    }

    // ── Copy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// HEBREW COUNTS ONE THING DIFFERENTLY FROM MANY, and these two lines are
    /// the ones a preview cap can force to "1".
    ///
    /// <para>"1 משימות נוספות" and "ועוד 1 צוותים" are the same error the
    /// overdue badge is not allowed to make — a numeral in front of a plural
    /// noun. Hebrew puts the number after the singular noun instead
    /// ("משימה אחת"), and for "one more" it drops the numeral entirely. The
    /// count is only ever ≥ 1 here: both call sites are guarded by
    /// <c>Count &gt; Preview</c>.</para></summary>
    private static string MoreTasksLabel(int n) =>
        n == 1 ? "+ משימה אחת נוספת" : $"+ {n} משימות נוספות";

    private static string MoreTeamsLabel(int n) =>
        n == 1 ? "ועוד צוות אחד" : $"ועוד {n} צוותים";

    private static string OneOf(string? first, string? second) =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(first)    ? first!.Trim()
        : !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(second) ? second!.Trim()
        : "";

    /// <summary>Join the parts that are actually present, so a row missing one
    /// has a shorter context line rather than a string of separators.</summary>
    private static string Join(params string?[] parts) =>
        string.Join(" · ", parts.Where(v => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(v)).Select(v => v!.Trim()));
}
